# Faultline — environment template. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored and is NEVER copied into an image (see .dockerignore). Every value
# here is a PLACEHOLDER — never commit real keys, ARNs, or account ids.
#
# Precedence for runtime/operational config: env var > `.env` > code default. (MODEL params —
# vols, spreads, scenarios — live separately in the governed configs/pricer/*.json, loaded via
# src/pricer/config.py, and are NOT set here.)
#
# Two settings namespaces:
#   * PRICER_*  — backend runtime (src/common/config/settings.py + src/pricer/settings.py,
#                 pydantic-settings, env_prefix="PRICER_"). Also read by the storage facade.
#   * QLP_*     — the UI BFF (ui/bff/app/settings.py).
#   * API_UPSTREAM — the UI (nginx) reverse-proxy target; substituted into the nginx config at
#                 container start (not baked into the JS bundle).
#
# On AWS these are rendered to an env file (e.g. /opt/qlp/.env) at instance boot from Secrets
# Manager / SSM Parameter Store; docker-compose.aws.yml loads it via `env_file`. S3 credentials
# are NEVER set here — boto3 uses the EC2 instance IAM role / the ambient AWS credential chain.
# See docs/guides/deployment_guide.md and docs/design/AITrade_aws_deployment_design.md.

# ── 1. Deploy mode & data location (dual-mode storage facade) ────────────────
# local (default) = the data root is <repo>/data on the local filesystem (byte-for-byte the
#                   historical behavior).
# aws             = data I/O routes to S3 via src/common/storage/.
PRICER_DEPLOY_MODE=local
# Data root. Local: a path (default <repo>/data when unset). AWS: an s3:// URI.
# REQUIRED when PRICER_DEPLOY_MODE=aws. S3 creds come from the instance role, NOT from here.
#PRICER_DATA_URI=s3://<data-bucket>/<prefix>

# ── 2. Backend runtime (PRICER_*) ───────────────────────────────────────────
PRICER_ENV=dev                       # dev | uat | prod — selects the optional pricer_config.<env>.json overlay
#PRICER_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
#PRICER_JSON_LOGS=true                # structured JSON logs (recommended in prod)
#PRICER_WORKERS=1                     # default parallelism for the runners (--workers overrides)
#PRICER_BOOK=core                     # active book variant: base|balanced|core|aggressive|risky (default = portfolio.json = core)

# ── 3. Service wiring & auth (endpoints + tokens; no data credentials) ───────
# Pricer FastAPI facade (src/pricer/service.py). When set, all routes except /health + /metrics
# require a matching `X-API-Key` header; unset = no-op (dev parity). Inject from Secrets Manager in prod.
#PRICER_API_KEY=<pricer-service-api-key>
# BFF (ui/bff): where it reads data + reaches the upstream pricer service.
QLP_ROOT=/app                        # data dir the BFF reads (repo root locally; an S3-synced / EFS mount in AWS)
QLP_SERVICE_URL=http://backend:8080  # upstream pricer API (only powers /system/health, /metrics + live re-price)
QLP_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8081   # comma-separated allowed origins (the UI's front-door origin)
#QLP_WRITE_TOKEN=<bff-write-token>    # locks the 4 gated writes (limits/signoff/jobs/sizing-activate). Inject in prod.
# UI (nginx) reverse-proxy target for /api → the BFF. Overridable per environment.
API_UPSTREAM=bff:8088

# ── 4. Scenariogen external services (dual-RAG + agentic LLM flow) ───────────
# Service ENDPOINTS are non-secret and env-overridable (configs/scenariogen/*.json use
# ${VAR:-default}); an unset var falls back to a localhost dev default, which FAILS in a container
# that has no such local service — set these to the in-VPC addresses in AWS. Forwarded into the
# backend container by docker-compose.aws.yml (CL-Q8).
#ARAG_BASE_URL=http://arag.internal:8001           # ARag REST (per-company Risk-Factor legs)
#MACRORAG_BASE_URL=http://macrorag.internal:8000   # MacroRAG REST (macro shock-vector legs)
#RAGINFER_URL=http://raginference.internal:8799    # shared bge embedder/reranker service
# Their API keys ARE secrets (inject from Secrets Manager); only needed if the service enforces auth.
#ARAG_API_KEY=<arag-api-key>
#MACRORAG_API_KEY=<macrorag-api-key>
# Scenariogen LLM flow (Mode-1/Mode-2 agentic scenario generation). UN-prefixed. The provider
# profile in configs/scenariogen/llm/llm.json picks the models: openai (default), anthropic or
# deepseek; the runner's --llm-profile overrides it. Only the keys of the providers the active
# profile uses are required (checked before a run). Each key also takes a <NAME>_FILE variant that
# points at a mounted secret file (Docker/K8s); the plain variable wins when both are set.
#SCENARIOGEN_LLM_PROFILE=openai
#OPENAI_API_KEY=<openai-api-key>
#OPENAI_API_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/openai_api_key
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=<anthropic-api-key>
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/anthropic_api_key
#DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=<deepseek-api-key>
#DEEPSEEK_API_KEY_FILE=/run/secrets/deepseek_api_key

# ── 5. Data-source API keys (market-data ingest; UN-prefixed) ────────────────
# Read by src/marketdata/common/settings.py (`load_credentials`) — NOT PRICER_-prefixed. A missing
# key only disables that source's ingest; pricing/risk never need one. Inject from Secrets Manager in prod.
#FAULTLINE_CONTACT_EMAIL=<your-email>  # contact in the User-Agent; REQUIRED by the SEC, GPR and EPU
#                                      # sources (they fail without it, per SEC fair-access policy)
#PENSFORD_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon-key> # scripts/rebuild_pensford_from_supabase.py; the public key from
#                                      # pensford.com/forward-curve (see the script's comment)
#FRED_API_KEY=<fred-api-key>          # FRED (rates / real-rate / throughput feeds)
#OPENFIGI_API_KEY=<openfigi-api-key>  # OpenFIGI (reference / identifier mapping)
#STOOQ_API_KEY=<stooq-api-key>        # Stooq (equity prices)
#FINRA_API_KEY=<finra-client-id>      # FINRA (F5 short-interest / crowding)
#FINRA_API_KEY_SECRET=<finra-secret>
#EIA_API_KEY=<eia-api-key>            # EIA (energy)

# ── 6. Build / image tags (used by docker-compose*.yml, not runtime settings) ─
#GIT_SHA=dev                          # baked into images as PRICER_GIT_SHA for run provenance (git rev-parse --short HEAD)
# ECR image URIs for the AWS overlay (docker-compose.aws.yml pulls these; unset = build locally):
#QLP_BACKEND_IMAGE=<acct>.dkr.ecr.<region>.amazonaws.com/qlp-backend:<tag>
#QLP_BFF_IMAGE=<acct>.dkr.ecr.<region>.amazonaws.com/qlp-bff:<tag>
#QLP_UI_IMAGE=<acct>.dkr.ecr.<region>.amazonaws.com/qlp-ui:<tag>
#QLP_ENV_FILE=/opt/qlp/.env           # env file the AWS overlay loads (rendered from Secrets Manager at boot)
